1. Suupose if we have parent object, then all the class extends parents should have override this method.

    ex: Class Bird -> fly() method and eat() method.

        1. Peigon  extends Bird-> as both fly() and eat() method is applicable.

        2. Sparrow extends Bird-> dont have fly() method, since sparrow cant fly. only have eat() method.


    -> Now if i do,  bird b = new Sparrow();
            b.fly();  -> it will give runtime exception.    because sparrow dont have fly method.

    -> According to LSP -> Child class should be replaceable with parent class without affecting the functionality of the program.



    -> Soln :   Create a seperate Interface -> Flyabble.

        1. Get fly method () from Bird and Add it to Flyabble interface.

        2. Now sparrow exteds Bird and dont implement Flyabble interface.

        3. Peigon extends Bird and implements Flyabble interface.

    -> Now Bird have only eat() method.

        Bird b = new Sparrow();
            b.eat();  -> it will work fine.   b.fly(),  we dont have it.

        Sparrow s = new Sparrow();
            s.eat();  -> it will work fine.     Follow LSP
            s.fly()  -> not support.